## Finding 1 — Time-to-discovery per quirk

Each quirk is measured **in isolation**: the simulator runs with exactly that
one quirk enabled and is reconciled against a control run in which every quirk
is off. That is a controlled experiment, and it is the only way "business days
until this behaviour surfaced" means what it says.

Business day 1 is the first business day of the window in which the quirk was
detected. Undetected quirks are shown, not hidden.

